 "checked": "Spain won the 2010 World Cup with Silva in the squad (Wikipedia x2). Valencia's debts: Villa to Barcelona for €40m, Silva sold too (Wikipedia Villa, Planet Football). Silva: Barcelona and Real Madrid interested (Silva interview via Wikipedia/90min), Chelsea courted him (mancity.com feature). Deal agreed 30 June 2010, about £25m/€30m (UEFA, AP). Hart: '£25 million, tiny, slow, only left footed' on the Kickback podcast (Goal, Football España). Mourinho Madrid coach from 31 May 2010 (Wikipedia). 2011-12 final table: City 89 (28-5-5, +64), United 89 (28-5-5, +56), Arsenal 70 (+25), Spurs 69 (+25) (Wikipedia, PL). Kompany header from Silva's corner, 30 April 2012, 45+1 (Sky, AP). Džeko headed in Silva's corner at 90+2 v QPR, Agüero won it at 93:20 (theScore, Planet Football). 436 games, 77 goals, 4 PL, 2 FA Cups, 5 League Cups (mancity.com, Irish Examiner). Statue unveiled 28 Aug 2021 (Irish Examiner, Sky). Real Madrid path imagined.",
